  "body": "Add a glossary page to the guide: one or two sentences per term, in CamCraft's own words, linking to the page that covers it in depth.\n\nStart with the terms the guide and the app use: setup, stock (and carried stock), model, part, WCS, work offset, operation, toolpath, generate, stale, verify, gouge, collision, refusal, rest material, holder and holder body, stick-out, stepover, stepdown, adaptive, finishing allowance, post (post processor, `.cps`), dialect / `capabilities`, setup sheet, reduced fidelity, live tooling, work spindle vs tool spindle, mill-turn, MCP.\n\nDefinitions are written from CamCraft's behaviour and general machining knowledge, not copied from other software's help (Clean-Room Protocol).\n\nDone means: a glossary page with at least 30 terms, each linked to its main page, linked from the guide index.\n",
